{
  "case_id": "2017-16-499",
  "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court Record",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nJEFFREY L. FISHER, Stanford, California; on behalf of the Petitioners.\nBRIAN H. FLETCHER, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, in support of neither party.\nPAUL D. CLEMENT, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Jeffrey L. Fisher)",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This Court made clear in Kiobel that the ATS should be construed first and foremost according to the ordinary rules of statutory construction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: How about Daimler?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What we allege is knowing and purposeful financing of terrorism with the expectation that it will make those terrorism attacks more successful and more lucrative for the perpetrators, and that is a violation of"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What -- what about another limitation that has been suggested, extraterritoriality, that's what this Court has declared. As there's a suggestion that perhaps there should be an exhaustion requirement, that is, you sue first in the country most concerned. You sue where this happened. And then, if you -- if you don't have a remedy in that most natural forum, then you can come here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bank",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the bank argued in the district court only that we should have brought this case in Jordan, and we responded to that argument with many, many problems with that suggestion. The district court rejected it. And the bank did not appeal that finding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: If I could understand what you're saying, you're saying that a norm is just a standard of conduct and doesn't have anything to with the enforcement of that standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLETCHER: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In the government's view, for some of the reasons that Justice Alito alluded to earlier, there's a serious question whether the claims in this case have a sufficient connection to the United States to proceed in U.S. court under the Alien Tort Statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case arises out of a suit by Israeli nationals against a corporation chartered in Jordan for injuries suffered in Israel and the adjoining territories. The defendant is not just chartered by the Kingdom of Jordan but it's closely regulated by Jordan and its central bank. Now, there are a host of problems with this lawsuit, not the least of which is there is nothing approaching a specific universal obligatory norm under international law that imposes obligations directly on corporations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: When you say that, I assumed, I take as a given, the statement in Sosa, does international law extend the scope of liability for a violation of a given norm to the perpetrator being sued, if the defendant is a private actor, such as a corporation or individual? That's the question you're addressing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Official International Convention for the Suppression of the Financing of Terrorism, which we've ratified, which says that states must take necessary measures to enable a legal entity located in its territory or organized under its laws to be held liable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I would tell you it's very important to read Article II and Article V in contradistinction with each other. And you will see that they are very different. Section 2, Article II makes it unlawful as a matter of international law, imposes a duty on a person. It doesn't define person, but then, if you look at Article V, it's crystal clear that the persons in Article II do not include legal entities that are addressed separately in Article V."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you give an example? Is there any place in the world that draws the distinction between individuals and corporations as far as liability for a violation of the law of nations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, all right. I quite agree with you. I looked at the footnote. And you can't get very far by pointing to six treaties that we didn't, nor others didn't sign."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you have something to gripe about as to this particular point, which is corporate versus individual liability?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under federal law? Wouldn't the individuals who were victimized have numerous other opportunities, numerous other ways to sue this American corporation for these torts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think it's an accident that each time you get one of these foreign cubed cases, that it's a foreign corporation, I don't think it's an accident that each time it comes up, it's really attractive to maybe duck the corporate liability question and decide the extraterritoriality question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, thank goodness we don't really have a lot of U.S. corporations that are violating international law right here in America, but if they did, there would be plenty of defendants under the ATS and under other provisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: There was some substantial -- there was a substantial sanction against this bank, wasn't there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Thank you. I'd like to turn to questions three Justices have asked, starting with Justice Kennedy, your question to me towards the end of my time about whether corporate liability falls on the conduct or enforcement side, and try to make two additional points about that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "former counter-terrorism officials",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0003-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the reason why, and this is laid out in the amicus brief from former counter-terrorism officials, is because Congress knew that aliens already had a cause of action under the ATS."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "is cited in the Solicitor General's brief dealing with the Little Tucker Act a few years ago, free and clear of all of the extraterritoriality concerns and everything else, just this Court straightforwardly said -\u00ad citing the provision there that said who could be sued, that that was part of the remedial structure of the Little Tucker Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0003-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, indeed, Congress made clear in the ATA that it was exercising its power under the define and punish clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0003-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: But why is that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-499",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "bb45a2d9736f5610db8b7c5b5698ca6ac206200c80efe05577e5fed817031fff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bb45a2d9736f-0003-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 12:03 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
